{Many, many more I probably haven't thought of.  This is where you
guys come in.  Have any other ideas?  I was thinking having a round
number of 100 total feats to accomplish.  Also, I haven't thought of
any of the in-game messages that should come up as a result of
accomplishing a feat.  Anyone have any good ones for the feats I've
listed above and the new ones you come up with on your own?}

As you can see, the point of the feats is to reward you for going out
of your way and doing things you wouldn't normally do.  The feats
would be designed such that none are mutually exclusive: it would be
possible, and therefore a new optional goal, to get every feat.

As it currently is, the only reason you'd not want to genocide certain
monsters is if you're going with extinctionless conduct.  That's not a
very good reason.  If, however, there were useful feats that could be
gained by not taking the chicken route of genociding the tough
species, then there might be less incentive to genocide everything
willy-nilly.

So, what do you think?  I might be interested in actually coding this
one up myself, if no one else beats me to it.  It would take a lot of
work though.

